TransactionChains::Vps::Replace::Os
  uses remote send steps for remote replace
  removes a group membership when the plan is unavailable in the destination environment
  marks the source as soft_delete, disables old resources, and schedules interface reassignment
  marks replacement dataset create hooks when existing backup paths will be preserved
  can leave existing backups on the original VPS when backup preservation is disabled
  does not mark replacement ancestors when only descendant backups will be preserved
  moves only the replaced group-snapshot membership between shared pool actions
  creates a destination group action and removes an orphaned source action
  adds a keep-going destination start when start is true
  fails when a hook creates a conflicting replacement backup dataset
  uses local copy for same-node replace and omits remote send steps
  copies only mounts for the root dataset and cloned descendants
  backs up replace snapshots, moves backup datasets, and rewires backup plans
  skips replacement mail when the user has the mailer disabled
  can move existing backups without creating replace-time backup snapshots

TransactionChains::Vps::Clone::OsToOs
  emits hostname changes and keeps universal resolvers untouched
  uses send transactions for remote clones and pins SendConfig payload
  copies dataset plans and dataset expansion histories when requested
  rejects cloned descendant diskspace that exceeds the user quota
  uses both user namespace maps and chowns when cloning to another owner
  clones descendant mounts, skips snapshot mounts, and ignores external mounts
  uses local copy for same-node clones and skips remote send steps
  keeps keep_snapshots=true as a pending contract until remote snapshot retention is wired (PENDING: keep_snapshots=true should preserve transfer snapshots, but the clone chain still appends source cleanup and the current node-side cleanup destroys those snapshots while closing the send state)
  does not register dataset plans when dataset_plans is false
  picks a resolver in the destination location for location-specific DNS
  clones interfaces, reallocates all IP resource buckets, and forwards address_location to allocation
  adds stop, sync, and source restart for consistent remote clones of running VPSes

TransactionChains::Vps::Swap
  rejects swap when network-interface topology does not match
  rejects swap between different owners
  rejects swap within the same location
  builds the expected broad migration and network-mutation subsequences for a cross-location swap

TransactionChains::Vps::Create
  deploys auto-add public keys and user data, then starts to apply NixOS user data even when start is false
  creates datasets, mounts, features, network configuration, DNS, and start in the expected order
  does not start when start is false and user data does not require apply
  prepares all requested address families before reserving any allocation
  raises when a template mount references a missing dataset

TransactionChains::Ip::Allocate
  returns fewer IPs with strict disabled when the pool runs out
  rechecks location after reserving a previously selected address
  rechecks purpose after reserving a previously selected address
  sets ownership when location IP ownership is enabled
  rejects a selected owned address whose current charge is in another environment
  adds auto host addresses when requested
  raises when strict allocation cannot find an address
  excludes disabled pools including owned detached reuse
  rejects a selected address outside its captured network identities
  updates all-vps exports with the allocated IP set
  selects an unowned candidate instead of an incompatible owned charge (ownership=true)
  reuses an owned allocation already charged in the destination without another charge
  selects an unowned candidate instead of an incompatible owned charge (ownership=false)
  rechecks owner after reserving a previously selected address
  does not widen a multi-address batch when another pool becomes enabled after its first reservation
  allocates routes with increasing order and charges the VPS environment
  rejects a stale selected address after its network is disabled
  rejects legacy owned addresses with no charge provenance
  treats an empty captured destination set as no capacity even with a populated continuity map

TransactionChains::Vps::Migrate
  builds a migration chain for VPSes with mounted subdatasets
  marks destination start as keep-going when skip_start is true
  replaces an IP using a candidate whose charge is compatible with the destination
  rejects migration of VPSes with multiple network interfaces
  returns OsToOs for vpsadminos to vpsadminos migrations
  queues the core os-to-os migration subsequence
  omits destination start when no_start is true
  rejects unsupported hypervisor combinations
  preserves all network interfaces and attached addresses during migration (PENDING: migration should preserve all interfaces and attached addresses, but Base#migrate_network_interfaces still rejects when the interface count exceeds one)
  rejects VPS migrations when the source subtree has snapshot clones

TransactionChains::Export::Create
  rechecks location after reserving a previously selected address
  rechecks purpose after reserving a previously selected address
  rechecks owner after reserving a previously selected address
  creates export runtime, hosts, and enable transactions for primary datasets
  uses a snapshot clone and sets expiration date when exporting a snapshot
  raises OperationNotSupported for datasets on unsupported pools
  allows a user-owned export server address on an export interface

